Contents of https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/javascript/api/@azure/keyvault-secrets/secretclient:
The SecretClient provides methods to manage [KeyVaultSecret](/en-us/javascript/api/@azure/keyvault-secrets/keyvaultsecret) in the Azure Key Vault. The client supports creating, retrieving, updating, deleting, purging, backing up, restoring and listing KeyVaultSecrets. The client also supports listing [DeletedSecret](/en-us/javascript/api/@azure/keyvault-secrets/deletedsecret) for a soft-delete enabled Azure Key Vault.

## Constructors

[SecretClient(string, TokenCredential, SecretClientOptions)](#@azure-keyvault-secrets-secretclient-constructor)

Creates an instance of SecretClient.

Example usage:

```
import { DefaultAzureCredential } from "@azure/identity";
import { SecretClient } from "@azure/keyvault-secrets";

const credential = new DefaultAzureCredential();

// Build the URL to reach your key vault
const vaultName = "<YOUR KEYVAULT NAME>";
const url = `https://${vaultName}.vault.azure.net`;

// Lastly, create our secrets client and connect to the service
const client = new SecretClient(url, credential);
```

