[purgeDeletedSecret(string, PurgeDeletedSecretOptions)](#@azure-keyvault-secrets-secretclient-purgedeletedsecret)

The purge deleted secret operation removes the secret permanently, without the possibility of recovery. This operation can only be enabled on a soft-delete enabled vault. This operation requires the secrets/purge permission.

Example usage:

```
import { DefaultAzureCredential } from "@azure/identity";
import { SecretClient } from "@azure/keyvault-secrets";

const credential = new DefaultAzureCredential();

const vaultName = "<YOUR KEYVAULT NAME>";
const url = `https://${vaultName}.vault.azure.net`;

const client = new SecretClient(url, credential);

const secretName = "MySecretName";

const deletePoller = await client.beginDeleteSecret(secretName);
await deletePoller.pollUntilDone();

await client.purgeDeletedSecret(secretName);
```

Permanently deletes the specified secret.

[restoreSecretBackup(Uint8Array, RestoreSecretBackupOptions)](#@azure-keyvault-secrets-secretclient-restoresecretbackup)

Restores a backed up secret, and all its versions, to a vault. This operation requires the secrets/restore permission.

Example usage:

```
import { DefaultAzureCredential } from "@azure/identity";
import { SecretClient } from "@azure/keyvault-secrets";

const credential = new DefaultAzureCredential();

const vaultName = "<YOUR KEYVAULT NAME>";
const url = `https://${vaultName}.vault.azure.net`;

const client = new SecretClient(url, credential);

const secretName = "MySecretName";

const backupResult = await client.backupSecret(secretName);

await client.restoreSecretBackup(backupResult);
```

Restores a backed up secret to a vault.

[setSecret(string, string, SetSecretOptions)](#@azure-keyvault-secrets-secretclient-setsecret)

The setSecret method adds a secret or secret version to the Azure Key Vault. If the named secret already exists, Azure Key Vault creates a new version of that secret. This operation requires the secrets/set permission.

Example usage:

```
import { DefaultAzureCredential } from "@azure/identity";
import { SecretClient } from "@azure/keyvault-secrets";

const credential = new DefaultAzureCredential();

const vaultName = "<YOUR KEYVAULT NAME>";
const url = `https://${vaultName}.vault.azure.net`;

const client = new SecretClient(url, credential);

const secretName = "MySecretName";

const result = await client.setSecret(secretName, "MySecretValue");
console.log("result: ", result);
```

Adds a secret in a specified key vault.

[updateSecretProperties(string, string, UpdateSecretPropertiesOptions)](#@azure-keyvault-secrets-secretclient-updatesecretproperties)

The updateSecret method changes specified attributes of an existing stored secret. Properties that are not specified in the request are left unchanged. The value of a secret itself cannot be changed. This operation requires the secrets/set permission.

Example usage:

```
import { DefaultAzureCredential } from "@azure/identity";
import { SecretClient } from "@azure/keyvault-secrets";

const credential = new DefaultAzureCredential();

const vaultName = "<YOUR KEYVAULT NAME>";
const url = `https://${vaultName}.vault.azure.net`;

const client = new SecretClient(url, credential);

const secretName = "MySecretName";

const result = await client.getSecret(secretName);
await client.updateSecretProperties(secretName, result.properties.version, { enabled: false });
```

Updates the attributes associated with a specified secret in a given key vault.

